Error [jet.NonCAbiType]: `#Export(c)` `twice` can fail: its body infers the carrier `Int Err!`, which is not a C-compatible return.
  --> tests/ui/cffi_e3203_export_inferred_failure.jet:6:12
    |
  6 | #Export(c) twice: fn(value: Int) -> Int {
    |            ^^^^^
 Why: `#Import` / `#Export` functions must use types with a stable C ABI at the edge, and a C caller has no failure channel.
 Fix: Handle every failure inside `twice` and declare it `Never!`.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3203
